Today, I learned about ELK Stack.

ELK Stack: ELK is a set of 3 open - source tools - Elastic Search, Logstash and Kibana - that work together to collect, search, analyze and visualize data in real time and together, they form a centrailized log management and analytics platform.

Elastic search: It is a distributed search engine and it stores all your logs.
Logstash: It is a data processing engine and it sends the data log to Elastic search.
Kibana: A web interface that plugin into Elastic search it lets you build intrative charts, graphs, maps and dasboard to exlpore your data visually.

